# List pagination (`Pagination`)

Use the shared **`Pagination`** component for **server-side** paginated lists. Do not build custom page controls or client-slice large datasets when the API already returns paginated rows.

**Component:** `front-end/src/components/common/Pagination.tsx`  
**Import:** `@/components/common/Pagination`  
**Meta type:** `@/shared/types/pagination` → `PaginationMeta`

## When to use

- Domain list pages (users, services, products, spaces, tags, webpages, etc.)
- Tab sections that fetch paginated data from the API (e.g. company product tabs)

Skip pagination UI when the endpoint returns all rows in one response and the list is intentionally small.

## UI placement

Inside the list body flex column, after the grid/list content:

```tsx
<div className="flex flex-col flex-1 min-h-0">
  <div className="flex-1">{/* grid or list */}</div>
  {pagination && (
    <div className="mt-auto pt-4">
      <Pagination
        totalItems={pagination.total}
        itemsPerPage={itemsPerPage}
        currentPage={currentPage}
        onPageChange={setCurrentPage}
        showItemsPerPageSelector={true}
        itemsPerPageOptions={[12, 24, 48, 96]}
        onItemsPerPageChange={(newItemsPerPage) => {
          setItemsPerPage(newItemsPerPage);
          setCurrentPage(1);
        }}
      />
    </div>
  )}
</div>
```

- Use `mt-auto pt-4` so pagination sticks to the bottom of the scroll area (see [list-page-shell.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/list-page-shell.mdc)).
- Optional guard: `pagination.total > 0` when the control should hide on empty results (see `UsersPage`).

## Component props

| Prop | Usage |
|------|--------|
| `totalItems` | `pagination.total` from API |
| `itemsPerPage` | Local state |
| `currentPage` | Local state (1-based) |
| `onPageChange` | Usually `setCurrentPage` |
| `showItemsPerPageSelector` | `true` on list pages |
| `itemsPerPageOptions` | `[12, 24, 48, 96]` for card/grid lists |
| `onItemsPerPageChange` | Update limit **and** reset `currentPage` to `1` |

Default component options (`[10, 20, 50, 100]`) are for generic use only — **list pages use `[12, 24, 48, 96]`**. Extract `ITEMS_PER_PAGE_OPTIONS` in the page hook when reused (see `useWebpagesPage.ts`).

## Page / hook state

Own pagination in the feature hook (`useSpacesPage`, `useUsersPage`, etc.):

```tsx
const [currentPage, setCurrentPage] = useState(1);
const [itemsPerPage, setItemsPerPage] = useState(12);
```

**Reset to page 1** when search or filters change:

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  setCurrentPage(1);
}, [debouncedSearchTerm, filterStatus /* other filter deps */]);
```

Also reset page 1 when header search or sessionStorage prefill applies a new query.

## Fetch / Redux wiring

Pass all three params on every fetch:

```tsx
const offset = (currentPage - 1) * itemsPerPage;
dispatch(fetchItemsRequest({
  limit: itemsPerPage,
  offset,
  page: currentPage,
  /* search + filters */
}));
```

- Store `pagination: PaginationMeta | null` in the feature slice; set it on fetch success.
- Render **API rows directly** — do not re-slice client-side when server pagination is active.
- Re-fetch after create/update/delete so `pagination.total` stays accurate (include current filters + page in the dispatch).

## Backend contract

Routes parse query params and models return a `pagination` object:

```js
const limit = parseInt(req.query.limit) || 12;
const offset = parseInt(req.query.offset) || 0;
const page = parseInt(req.query.page) || Math.floor(offset / limit) + 1;
```

Response shape (see `PaginationMeta`):

```json
{
  "total": 42,
  "limit": 12,
  "offset": 0,
  "totalPages": 4,
  "currentPage": 1
}
```

- Cap `limit` in Joi (typically max `100`; appointments may allow higher for dashboards).
- Empty results still return `pagination` with `total: 0`.

